      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCKINWITHATTITUDE (7) was just too classy in her resuming win at Melton, leading to score by close to 9m. Starts from a 30m handicap but strikes at 50 per cent when second-up and owns a strong record at this venue. Terrific mare who is the one to beat. IMPERIAL MONARCH NZ (6) made an encouraging return when runner-up at Melton last week, continuing a string of placings from last campaign. Won over this distance the only time he raced here. Fitter so looks a threat. MEADOW VALLEY STAR (5) had some decent form last time in. Hasn't raced since April but is a two-time fresh winner and was readied with a trial. ANTONOV NZ (2) jumps in grade but deserves respect having won his last two outings from standing starts.",
